    Bug 2047449 - Don't notify copy service listeners during XPCOM shutdown. r=mkmelin


    During ~nsMsgCopyService() (XPCOM shutdown), ClearRequest() was notifying
    listeners of failure. nsMsgFilterAfterTheFact::OnStopCopy() responded by
    calling ContinueExecutionPrompt(), which uses mozilla::intl::Localization
    (Fluent) to localize a dialog string. The Rust L10nRegistry panics with
    "Failed to retrieve app locales" because locale services are already torn
    down at this point — a regression from the Fluent migration in bug 2012697.

    Null the listener before ClearRequest() in the destructor so no
    notification is sent. No useful work can be done by listeners during
    teardown anyway.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306638

diff --git a/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgCopyService.cpp b/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgCopyService.cpp
index dcb5d2f0a5c..2fdebd50160 100644
--- a/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgCopyService.cpp
+++ b/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgCopyService.cpp
@@ -8,7 +8,6 @@
 #include "nsIFile.h"
 #include "nsIMsgFolderNotificationService.h"
 #include "nsIMsgTransactionService.h"
-#include "nsServiceManagerUtils.h"
 #include "nsMsgUtils.h"
 #include "mozilla/Components.h"
 #include "mozilla/Logging.h"
@@ -107,7 +106,13 @@ nsMsgCopyService::nsMsgCopyService() {}
 nsMsgCopyService::~nsMsgCopyService() {
   int32_t i = m_copyRequests.Length();

-  while (i-- > 0) ClearRequest(m_copyRequests.ElementAt(i), NS_ERROR_FAILURE);
+  while (i-- > 0) {
+    nsCopyRequest* req = m_copyRequests.ElementAt(i);
+    // Don't notify listeners during XPCOM shutdown; services they depend on
+    // (localization, prompts, etc.) may already be torn down.
+    req->m_listener = nullptr;
+    ClearRequest(req, NS_ERROR_FAILURE);
+  }
 }

